From f86da7ea6a1691a8852ff0339539169880783c8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claudio Terzi <ilclaudioterzi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:02:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] slo: flag truncated sources, the mirror case of the
 silent-zero canary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SLO module's docstring says its job is catching "silent zero" — a
source that stops flowing and reports 0 rows, which reads as "nothing
happened" rather than "nothing arrived". This adds the mirror case.

fetch_firms_fires caps the global VIIRS CSV at the top 5000 hotspots by
FRP, which is a sensible rendering budget — the map cannot usefully draw
every thermal anomaly on the planet. But len(all_rows) is then discarded,
so downstream len(latest_data["firms_fires"]) returns 5000 and is
indistinguishable from a real measurement. /api/health reports it as a
count. On a normal day the global 24h feed carries several times that,
so the dashboard shows a ceiling where an operator reads a total.

Same shape as `empty`, opposite direction: a number that means something
other than what it appears to mean.

Changes, all additive and backward compatible:

- _store: source_totals dict plus _mark_total(source, total) and
  get_source_totals_snapshot(), mirroring source_timestamps/_mark_fresh.
  A fetcher that caps records the upstream count before truncating.
- earth_observation: fetch_firms_fires records len(all_rows); the country
  enrichment path updates the figure after its own 6000 merge cap. Both
  caps are now named constants instead of inline literals, and the log
  line reports stored-of-upstream with a [TRUNCATED] marker.
- slo.compute_status: optional total_rows parameter; when it exceeds
  row_count the entry gains total_rows and truncated=True. Sources that
  never cap get no new keys at all, so a caller cannot mistake absence
  for truncated=False. compute_all_statuses takes an optional third
  argument; existing two-argument callers are unaffected.
- routers/health: passes the totals snapshot through.

row_count is left exactly as it was. It is still the number of rows
stored; the addition only lets a consumer learn that it is a floor.

Tests in backend/tests/test_slo_truncation.py cover both directions, the
no-total case, the unconfigured-source case, and the backward-compatible
two-argument call.
---
